  "notes": "Intransitive verb. Takes the particle に to indicate the state being entered. Almost always used with negative or undesirable states.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- パニックに{陥|おちい}る (to fall into panic)\n- {混乱|こんらん}に{陥|おちい}る (to fall into confusion)\n- {危機|きき}に{陥|おちい}る (to fall into crisis)\n- {悪循環|あくじゅんかん}に{陥|おちい}る (to fall into a vicious cycle)\n- {罠|わな}に{陥|おちい}る (to fall into a trap)\n- {苦境|くきょう}に{陥|おちい}る (to fall into difficulty)\n\nCOMMON PATTERNS:\nPattern: ～に{陥|おちい}る. The に marks the state or condition that the subject falls into. Unlike {落|お}ちる (to physically fall), {陥|おちい}る is used for abstract or situational \"falling.\"",
